 {r}←SetDebug (logging suspend trace);logging;suspend;trace
⍝ Configure DCMS debug controls and propagate them to Stark (router) and Jarvis.
⍝
⍝ logging  ∈ 0 1     : whether Log lines print to the session
⍝ suspend  ∈ 0 1 2   : which classes of error suspend (vs trap into a response):
⍝                        0 = none     (expected → response, bugs → 500 response)
⍝                        1 = bugs     (expected → response, bugs → suspend)
⍝                        2 = all      (all errors suspend)
⍝ trace    ∈ 0 1     : whether to suspend on request entry to step through a request

 :If ~(logging∊0 1)∧(suspend∊0 1 2)∧(trace∊0 1)
     ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message' 'SetDebug: settings must be (logging∊0 1)(suspend∊0 1 2)(trace∊0 1)')
 :EndIf
⍝ DCMS-level controls (the values HandleError and Log read)
 GLOBAL.logging←logging
 GLOBAL.suspend←suspend
 GLOBAL.trace←trace
 :If 0=GLOBAL.⎕NC'log'
     GLOBAL.log←''
 :EndIf
⍝ SQL verbose output follows logging
 :If 0≠⎕NC'SQL'
     SQL.debug←logging
 :EndIf
⍝ Propagate to the framework if it is up. router.Debug / jarvis.Debug are bitmasks:
⍝   bit 1  (value 1)  — stop on error (disables :Trap so the error suspends)
⍝   bit 64 (value 64) — Stark: stop before routing (request-entry trace)
⍝ Keep Stark's dispatch trap ON unless suspend=2, so HandleError still runs to
⍝ classify and respond to expected errors; route unexpected bugs to the debugger
⍝ via Jarvis (bit 1) when suspend>0.
 :If 0≠⎕NC'router'
     router.Debug←(1×2=suspend)+(64×trace)
 :EndIf
 :If 0≠⎕NC'jarvis'
     jarvis.Debug←1×suspend>0   ⍝ MUST be set after router.Start (Stark forwards bit 1)
 :EndIf
 ⎕←'[DEBUG] logging=',(⍕logging),' suspend=',(⍕suspend),' trace=',⍕trace
 r←logging suspend trace
